From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: a bounded wait for the Wine Mono installer

When no Wine Mono is found, mscoree's registration (as wineboot -u runs it) starts appwiz.cpl install_mono and waited for it without a bound; appwiz's download dialog waits for an answer, so a prefix update could block for ever on a display nobody watches. mscoree now waits 120 seconds and goes on; the dialog stays up for whoever can answer it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mscoree/mscoree_main.c b/dlls/mscoree/mscoree_main.c
index 219330a..f6c798d 100644
--- a/dlls/mscoree/mscoree_main.c
+++ b/dlls/mscoree/mscoree_main.c
@@ -896,7 +896,14 @@ static BOOL invoke_appwiz(void)
     free(args);
     if (ret) {
         CloseHandle(pi.hThread);
+        /* appwiz may wait on its download dialog: a prefix update (wineboot -u) waits for it a
+         * bounded time, then goes on; the dialog stays for whoever can answer it */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_APPWIZ_WAIT_FOREVER
+        if (WaitForSingleObject(pi.hProcess, 120000) == WAIT_TIMEOUT)
+            WARN("appwiz.cpl install_mono still running after 120 s, not waiting for it\n");
+#else
         WaitForSingleObject(pi.hProcess, INFINITE);
+#endif
         CloseHandle(pi.hProcess);
     }
 
